{#
    "My Times" — a coach's recurring weekly availability (FR-082, FR-087, US-01.10).

    The same grid the family sees, on the coach's own subject. Split shifts need no special
    control: two runs of ticked hours with a gap between them are stored as two ranges, and two
    adjacent runs become one.

    The overrides table below is as far as FR-087 goes in this task, and the template says so
    where a reader will ask. "The coach sees the assignment" needs Epic-02's assignments to exist,
    and "can accept or request a change" has no defined workflow, recipient or state anywhere in
    the spec (G-30) — so what a coach gets today is the honest record that a trainer scheduled
    them outside their times, and why.
#}
{% extends 'coach/_layout.html.twig' %}
{% form_theme form 'account/_form_theme.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}My Times{% endblock %}
{% block heading %}My Times{% endblock %}

{% block coach_content %}

    <p class="muted">
        Trainers see these times when they schedule sessions. They are a guide: a trainer can
        still ask you to cover a session outside them, and you will see their reason here.
    </p>

    {{ include('availability/_summary.html.twig', {summary: summary}) }}

    {% if weekLines is not empty %}
        <ul class="week-lines">
            {% for line in weekLines %}<li>{{ line }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% endif %}

    {{ form_start(form, {attr: {'data-availability-form': ''}}) }}
        {{ include('account/_error_summary.html.twig', {form: form}) }}

        {{ include('availability/_grid.html.twig', {form: form, days: days, grid: grid}) }}

        <div class="actions">
            <button class="pp-btn pp-btn--primary" type="submit">Save my times</button>
            <button type="button" data-availability-copy-weekdays hidden>Copy Monday to all weekdays</button>
            <button type="button" data-availability-clear hidden>Clear all</button>
        </div>

        {{ form_rest(form) }}
    {{ form_end(form, {render_rest: false}) }}

    <h2>Sessions scheduled outside your times</h2>

    {% if overrides is empty %}
        <p class="muted">Nothing yet. When a trainer schedules you outside these times, their reason appears here.</p>
    {% else %}
        <table class="overrides">
            <caption class="visually-hidden">Overrides recorded against your availability</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">When</th>
                    <th scope="col">Session time</th>
                    <th scope="col">Recorded by</th>
                    <th scope="col">Reason</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for override in overrides %}
                    <tr>
                        <td>{{ override.createdAt|date('Y-m-d H:i') }}</td>
                        <td>{{ override.dayOfWeek.label }} {{ override.window.format }}</td>
                        <td>{{ override.overriddenBy.displayName }}</td>
                        <td>{{ override.reason }}</td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
